X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Undocu Bienestar Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T190000
DTSTAMP:20260424T115510Z
UID:20260507T000000Z-18384@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T170000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,3200,3200/610_cs_-_Rosco_Roseland_2026_03_OK_067.rev
 .1777057435.jpg
CATEGORIES:Department Events,Student Services
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with SRJC Student Health Services and SRJC Rose
 land\, we are pleased to invite you and your students to the Undocu Bienes
 tar Celebration\, the culminating event of our Undocu Bienestar series. Th
 is initiative was made possible through a grant from CalMHSA (https://www.
 calmhsa.org/).&#160\;Schedule:  • 5:00–5:30 PM: Danza Xantolt   5:00
 –7:00 PM: Food\, music\, and wellness resources  • 5:30–7:00 PM: Wor
 kshop – No Borders to Our Belonging: "Cuerpo Territorio" (hosted by Bota
 nical Bus (https://thebotanicalbus.org/))Workshop Description  No Borders 
 to Our Belonging: "Cuerpo Territorio" is a bilingual wellness workshop des
 igned to cultivate a sense of radical belonging within immigrant communiti
 es through connection to the earth and to one another. The session will be
  facilitated in Spanish and English by two Promotora Community Health Work
 ers trained in trauma-informed care.  Please note that workshop participat
 ion is limited to 30 attendees. We encourage early arrival to secure a spo
 t.To learn more click here! (https://dream.santarosa.edu/workshops-events-
 2025-2026)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260430T202927Z
LOCATION:SRJC Roseland
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18384-undocu-bienestar-celebratio
 n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In partnership with SRJC Student Health 
 Services and SRJC Roseland\, we are pleased to invite you and your student
 s to the Undocu Bienestar Celebration\, the culminating event of our Undoc
 u Bienestar series. This initiative was made possible through a grant from
  <a href="https://www.calmhsa.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CalMHSA
 </a>.&#160\;</p><p><strong>Schedule</strong>:<br />  • 5:00–5:30 PM: D
 anza Xantolt<br />  • 5:00–7:00 PM: Food\, music\, and wellness resour
 ces<br />  • 5:30–7:00 PM: Workshop – No Borders to Our Belonging: "
 Cuerpo Territorio" (hosted by <a href="https://thebotanicalbus.org/" targe
 t="_blank" rel="noopener">Botanical Bus</a>)</p><p><strong>Workshop Descri
 ption</strong><br />  No Borders to Our Belonging: "Cuerpo Territorio" is 
 a bilingual wellness workshop designed to cultivate a sense of radical bel
 onging within immigrant communities through connection to the earth and to
  one another. The session will be facilitated in Spanish and English by tw
 o Promotora Community Health Workers trained in trauma-informed care.</p><
 p>  Please note that <strong>workshop participation is limited</strong> to
  30 attendees. We encourage early arrival to secure a spot.</p><p><a href=
 "https://dream.santarosa.edu/workshops-events-2025-2026" target="_blank" r
 el="noopener">To learn more click here!</a></p>
