DESCRIPTION:This free conference will bring together students\, educators\
 , and community partners to explore pathways in healthcare and highlight c
 ulturally responsive practices in health and wellness. A special feature o
 f the event will be our student poster presentations from 10:00 – 11:00 
 AM\, showcasing a wide range of student research across disciplines. This 
 portion\, along with tabling from local organizations\, will be open to al
 l with no registration required.  From 11:00 AM – 2:00 PM\, registered a
 ttendees will participate in the main program in Lindley 138\, featuring a
  keynote speaker\, a professional panel\, and a human resources panel. The
  conference will conclude with lunch and a live Norteño band from 2:00 
 – 3:00 PM in the Lindley Quad.For more information\, and to register to 
 attend the Speaker Sessions click here! (https://hope.santarosa.edu/camino
 s-en-salud-conference)
