SUMMARY:Inner Body Guided-Meditation 
DESCRIPTION:The Mindful Stream (CA)\n"Awareness of the inner body takes yo
 u beyond the mind." - Eckhart Tolle\n\nIn this mediation session we will b
 ring our attention here: to the inner body where we practise presence by f
 ocusing on our physical sensations.\n\nSessions are suitable for newcomers
 \, those experienced in Tolle's teachings and anyone wishing to remain com
 pletely anonymous. They will last around 20 minutes and cameras and microp
 hones will be disabled. (Depending on the situation\, a free discussion ma
 y be held at the end with mics and cameras allowed.)\n\nSessions are suita
 ble for newcomers\, those experienced in Tolle's teachings and anyone wish
 ing to remain completely anonymous. They will last around 20 minutes and c
 ameras and microphones will be disabled. (Depending on the situation\, a f
 ree discussion may be held at the end with mics and cameras allowed.)\n\nS
 ee you there!\n\nEmrys also organises a free Work of Byron Katie online me
 diation group. Visit [this Meetup Group link](https://www.meetup.com/thewo
 rk-runsfree/) for more information.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/mindfulnesspetaluma/events/314364753/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260419T145931Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260419T145931Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Sonoma County Go Wild Hikers": "https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/events/314407679/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_sonoma_county_go_wild_hikers
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Go Wild Hikers
UID:event_314407679@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260505T032137Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T113000
SUMMARY:Vista Trail at Sugarloaf
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nWe never get tired of hiking Sugarloaf. This i
 s a very popular park with rolling hills\, dense forests\, creeks\, wildfl
 owers & waterfalls (in season). We'll hike up to Vista Trail while taking 
 in the beauty. Then hike back down past Sonoma Creek. Appropriate for indi
 viduals with at least a moderate level of fitness.\n\n**\\*Important Notic
 e\\***\nIf you've enjoyed hiking with this group follow me as I move Go Wi
 ld Hikers to a new platform by the end of May\, called Heylo at - https://
 heylo.com/invite/PpURbZWX\nClick on the link above to join.\n\n**Where We 
 Meet/Important Directions**\nSugarloaf Ridge State Park\n2605 Adobe Canyon
  Road\, Kenwood\, 95452\n**Get there Early! Carpool if you can - This is a
  very Popular Park!**\nGive yourself enough time to arrive\, use the restr
 oom & pay park fee. It often takes longer than you think.\n**Meet in large
  parking lot on the left after passing entrance/Pay Kiosk!**\n\n**The Hike
  (Group Hike #342)**\nLower Bald Mtn\, Bald Mountain\, Vista\, Meadow and 
 Creekside Nature Trails - a loop hike\nDistance - +/-4.75 miles/+/-7.6 kil
 ometers\nElevation change - +/-800 feet/+/-244 meters\nDifficulty - 7/10 m
 oderate with some steep sections\nExposures - 40% shade/60 % sun - rocky\,
  poison oak\, ticks and insects\nBring plenty of water - at least 34 oz./ 
 1 liter\nDogs - Not permitted\nFacilities at trail head - shade\, picnic t
 ables and toilets\nCost - $5 cash\nParking - $10 State Park fee or free wi
 th your State Park Pass.\nRemember to wear appropriate hiking shoes\, brin
 g plenty of water\, a hat\, a snack and layered clothing.\nPlease Do Not U
 se Any scented products the day of a group hike!\nOf course we will all lo
 ok out for each other but ultimately\, hikers are responsible for their ow
 n safety and well-being during hikes.\n\nSarmentine French Bakery/Cafe\n(N
 ear McDonald's)\n52 Mission Circle\, Suite # 112\nSanta Rosa\, CA 95409\n[
 (707) 623-9595](https://www.google.com/search?q=sarmentine+alexandra&sourc
 e=lmns&bih=768&biw=1342&client=safari&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwizy6KH0v6AAxWs
 IkQIHb4UA3cQ0pQJKAB6BAgBEAI#)\n[https://www.sarmentine.com/](https://www.s
 armentine.com/)\n\n**When We Meet**\nSaturday May 9\, 2026\n8:30 am - 11:3
 0 am\n**Get there Early! Carpool if you can - This is a very Popular Park!
 **\nIf your plans change after you sign up even if you're on the waitlist\
 , please update your RSVP.\nDo Not Attend if you are sick\, running a feve
 r\, were exposed to or have tested positive for Covid-19 or any other cont
 agion!\nHike may be changed\, rescheduled or cancelled in case of excessiv
 e heat\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apocalypse etc... Check your 
 email the night before for any possible changes.\n\n**Notice to New Hikers
  Only**\n**"When a New Hiker (never hiked with me before) doesn't show up 
 (No Show) to their first hike with the group\, they will be removed (not b
