ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,596,596/611_cs_-_spring_2026_dance_show.rev.17774125
 69.png
CATEGORIES:Dance,Theatre Arts
DESCRIPTION:Make It COUNT brings together faculty choreography\, student w
 orks\, and selected solos\, duets\, and trios in a vibrant concert that hi
 ghlights the creativity and versatility of SRJC dancers. From mathematical
  patterns and sequences to personal stories tied to age\, time\, and data\
 , each piece offers a unique interpretation of how numbers shape our world
 .  The concert also features guest artists bringing exciting new voices to
  the stage. Farrah McAdam celebrates Bruno Mars' discography through a dyn
 amic jazz-funk set\, while Bernadette Alverio of The Movement Lab explores
  an edgy modern piece centered around the concept of "9 lives."  The progr
 am showcases a range of styles including contemporary\, modern\, jazz\, an
 d experimental dance\, reflecting the diverse voices within the department
 . In addition to performance\, the production emphasizes mentorship\, coll
 aboration\, and professional development\, giving students hands-on experi
 ence in choreography\, rehearsal process\, and live theater production.Buy
  tickets here! (https://www.srjcathletics.com/Athletic_Tickets)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T215153Z
LOCATION:Burbank Theater - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18583-make-it-count-spring-2026-d
 ance-show
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Make It COUNT</em> brings together fac
 ulty choreography\, student works\, and selected solos\, duets\, and trios
  in a vibrant concert that highlights the creativity and versatility of SR
 JC dancers. From mathematical patterns and sequences to personal stories t
 ied to age\, time\, and data\, each piece offers a unique interpretation o
 f how numbers shape our world.</p><p>  The concert also features guest art
 ists bringing exciting new voices to the stage. Farrah McAdam celebrates B
 runo Mars' discography through a dynamic jazz-funk set\, while Bernadette 
 Alverio of The Movement Lab explores an edgy modern piece centered around 
 the concept of "9 lives."</p><p>  The program showcases a range of styles 
 including contemporary\, modern\, jazz\, and experimental dance\, reflecti
 ng the diverse voices within the department. In addition to performance\, 
 the production emphasizes mentorship\, collaboration\, and professional de
 velopment\, giving students hands-on experience in choreography\, rehearsa
 l process\, and live theater production.</p><p><a href="https://www.srjcat
 hletics.com/Athletic_Tickets" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy tickets h
 ere!</a></p>
