SUMMARY:Immigrant Pathways to Economic Mobility - 2026 Del Monte Lecture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T130000
DTSTAMP:20260416T142217Z
UID:20260512T190000Z-18025@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T120000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,262,262/596_dr_marlene_orozco.rev.1776373414.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events,District Events
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to attend the 2026 Del Monte Lecture hosted by
  the SRJC Foundation.  "Immigrant Pathways to Economic Mobility - The Role
  of Education\, Workforce Development\, and Entrepreneurship"  This year's
  featured speaker\, Dr. Marlene Orozco\, is a nationally recognized resear
 cher in economic mobility\, entrepreneurship\, and equity. Her talk will c
 onnect national research with local impact\, highlighting how immigrants c
 ontribute to Sonoma County's economy and the critical role SRJC plays in c
 reating pathways through education\, career training\, and entrepreneurshi
 p.  This lecture offers an opportunity to:  • Engage with research that 
 aligns with our work across instruction\, student services\, and workforce
  development  • Reflect on how our programs support economic mobility an
 d community vitality  • Connect with colleagues\, students\, and communi
 ty partners around a shared topic of impact  The event is free and open to
  all\; we encourage you to attend.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T170924Z
LOCATION:Frank Chong Black Box Theatre\, Burbank Auditorium - Santa Rosa C
 ampus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18025-immigrant-pathways-to-econo
 mic-mobility-2026-del-monte
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  You are invited to attend the 2026 Del M
 onte Lecture hosted by the SRJC Foundation.</p><p>  "Immigrant Pathways to
  Economic Mobility - The Role of Education\, Workforce Development\, and E
 ntrepreneurship"</p><p>  This year's featured speaker\, Dr. Marlene Orozco
 \, is a nationally recognized researcher in economic mobility\, entreprene
 urship\, and equity. Her talk will connect national research with local im
 pact\, highlighting how immigrants contribute to Sonoma County's economy a
 nd the critical role SRJC plays in creating pathways through education\, c
 areer training\, and entrepreneurship.<br />  This lecture offers an oppor
 tunity to:<br />  • Engage with research that aligns with our work acros
 s instruction\, student services\, and workforce development<br />  • Re
 flect on how our programs support economic mobility and community vitality
 <br />  • Connect with colleagues\, students\, and community partners ar
 ound a shared topic of impact<br />  The event is free and open to all\; w
 e encourage you to attend.</p>
